{% comment %}
    A radio group rendered as tiles, for a short set of values that carry an
    icon and a colour elsewhere in the app — severity, remediation status,
    visibility. A plain select spells those out as bare words, which makes the
    reader translate "medium" into the amber badge they will see afterwards;
    here the option already looks like the badge.

    Use it for up to about six options that fit on one line each. More than that,
    or free text, belongs in `select`.

    Params:
      name      field name shared by every radio
      options   list of {value, label, icon, variant, disabled}, where `variant`
                is a badge family — primary, secondary, success, warning, danger,
                info, violet, severity-critical/high/medium/low
      selected  the value that starts checked
      label     group label
      hint      helper line under the group
      required  marks the group required
      class     extra classes on the wrapper
{% endcomment %}
<div class="space-y-1.5{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}">
    {% if label %}
        <span class="tw-form-label">
            {{ label }}
            {% if required %}<span class="text-danger">*</span>{% endif %}
        </span>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="tw-choice-group"
         role="radiogroup"
         {% if label %}aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %}
         {{ attrs|safe }}>
        {% for option in options %}
            <label class="tw-choice{% if option.variant %} tw-choice-{{ option.variant }}{% endif %}">
                <input type="radio"
                       name="{{ name }}"
                       value="{{ option.value }}"
                       {% if option.value == selected %}checked{% endif %}
                       {% if option.disabled %}disabled{% endif %}
                       {% if required %}required{% endif %}>
                {% if option.icon %}<i class="{{ option.icon }} tw-choice-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>{% endif %}
                <span>{{ option.label }}</span>
            </label>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% if hint %}<p class="tw-form-hint">{{ hint }}</p>{% endif %}
</div>
